WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.560
When a bottle of ethanoyl chloride is opened,
fumes start to curl out of its neck.

2
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.880
On paper, it is almost ethanoic acid.

3
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.100
Just one group has been
swapped for a chlorine atom.

4
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.780
Yet a bottle of ethanoic acid
just sits there, quiet and still.

5
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.380
Two near-identical liquids.

6
00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:23.620
So why does one fume in moist air,
while the other does nothing?

7
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:29.140
In this mission, you'll meet the acid
derivatives, from acyl chlorides to amides.

8
00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.380
Then you'll react ethanoyl
chloride with alcohols,

9
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.880
ammonia and amines, and name each product.

10
00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:40.360
Your mission: explain why ethanoyl
chloride fumes in moist air,

11
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.190
while ethanoic acid does not. 